{"title":"ECG/Echo Technician Roadmap","role":"ECG/Echo Technician","summary":"An ECG/Echo Technician is an allied healthcare professional who performs and supports non-invasive cardiovascular diagnostic procedures, primarily electrocardiography (ECG) and echocardiography (Echo).","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Cardiac Care / Cardiovascular Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An ECG/Echo Technician is an allied healthcare professional who performs and supports non-invasive cardiovascular diagnostic procedures, primarily electrocardiography (ECG) and echocardiography (Echo)."},{"type":"p","text":"The professional works with cardiologists and clinical teams to acquire high-quality cardiac diagnostic data."},{"type":"p","text":"Core areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"12-lead ECG"},{"text":"Rhythm monitoring"},{"text":"Holter monitoring"},{"text":"Exercise/stress testing support"},{"text":"Echocardiography assistance"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Cardiac diagnostic equipment"},{"text":"Basic cardiac anatomy and physiology"},{"text":"Emergency cardiac-care awareness"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Infection control"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"Performing diagnostic tests and interpreting them are different responsibilities. The technician's primary role is accurate test acquisition, technical quality and patient support; formal clinical interpretation is generally performed by an appropriately qualified clinician."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus","Career Outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, cardiac foundations"},{"text":"Strong clinical foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"ECG and cardiovascular diagnostics"},{"text":"Core ECG competence"}],[{"te